      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're on the right track with the high protein diet, but you need to be careful with the aged cheddar and salami. Those are high in tyramine, which can interact with your MAOI medication and cause a serious serotonin surge. I recommend sticking to low-tyramine protein sources like chicken, fish, and tofu. And don't worry about the soy sauce, a little bit of it won't hurt. Just be sure to cook it down to a sauce-like consistency to minimize the tyramine content.",
